// Client-scoped derivation of the `scsi` dataset — NOT a second copy.
//
// This inherits every model, relationship, metric and description from `scsi` and adds one
// thing: the row-level restriction. Anything added to `scsi` appears here automatically,
// so the two cannot drift.
//
// WHY A SEPARATE DATASET AT ALL:
// Holistics evaluates row-level permission at the dataset level, and an embed token can
// only supply VALUES to a permission the dataset already declares — it cannot create the
// filter itself. So a single shared dataset carrying `client_scope` would restrict internal
// staff too, and every internal non-Admin user would need `scsi_client_id` provisioned as the
// "All" value type just to see their own agency's data. Anyone missed would silently get an
// empty dashboard — no error, no signal.
//
// Splitting the restriction into this derivation makes the internal/external boundary a
// property of the model rather than of per-user setup:
//   scsi         → unscoped → internal reporting (scsi_collections_analytics)
//   scsi_client  → scoped   → external portal    (scsi_client_portal, scsi_portal)
//
// Column-level PHI redaction is NOT here: it lives on the public_accounts model
// (`debtor_state_pii`), so it applies to both datasets automatically and composes with,
// rather than duplicates, this restriction.
Dataset scsi_client = scsi.extend({
  label: 'SCSI Collections (Client-Scoped)'

  // Row-level scoping for the external client portal: a provider organisation sees only
  // the accounts it placed with the agency. Rows are medical-debt PHI and the agency is a
  // HIPAA Business Associate of the placing provider.
  //
  // The dedicated `scsi_client_id` user attribute avoids colliding with the unrelated
  // `company_id` id-space used by the Brainstorm APAC demo.
  //
  // Scoping on accounts (not clients) is deliberate: payments and contact_attempts inherit
  // the restriction through their joins to accounts, so no child row escapes it.
  //
  // Not enforced for Admins or Analysts with data source access.
  // NOTE: RLS-as-code must be enabled for this tenant and only takes effect after publish.
  permission client_scope {
    field: r(public_accounts.client_id)
    operator: 'matches_user_attribute'
    value: 'scsi_client_id'
  }
})
